rcq("R08-C-08-4", "Except / not supported", "Difficult",
    "Each of the following is consistent with the author's argument EXCEPT:",
    "The decline of the mass audience is to be regretted mainly because it ended the experience of a nation attending to the same events.",
    [("Groups that read quite different publications may still resolve their factual disputes with one another if they accept the same rules of evidence.",
      "Paragraph 4 says such a society 'is plural, not broken', so this is consistent with the argument."),
     ("A shared body of reported facts, even one assembled selectively, made it easier for political opponents to argue usefully about policy.",
      "Paragraph 3 grants that a shared stock of facts 'gave opponents something definite to disagree about'."),
     ("An attempt to restore a few dominant news outlets could also bring back the exclusions that once accompanied their authority.",
      "Paragraph 5 says nostalgia 'risks restoring the exclusions along with the authority', so this matches.")],
    "Paragraph 3 says what was lost 'was not chiefly that everyone attended to the same things', which 'was never a requirement of self-government'; the real loss was shared procedures for settling disputes of fact. Locating the main regret in common attention contradicts this.",
    "Accepting this statement because the author does admit a genuine loss, without noticing that the author locates that loss elsewhere.",
    "The key overlaps the author's concession; rejecting it requires the precise 'not chiefly' distinction of paragraph 3.",
    cognitive="Analysis", exams=DX)

